what is the meaning of The White Buffalo  who is the monocle what's Harlan like as  an old man here are the small details  you missed in the Umbrella Academy  Season 3.  for those unfamiliar with the Umbrella  Academy Source material the comic book  series by Gerard Way and Gabrielle ba  that began publishing in 2007 the hotel  Oblivion is a direct reference to the My  Chemical Romance front man's third  volume of the family's Story the moment  in this scene that we are referencing  here though is a tip of the cap to the  opening of Orson Welles 1941 classic  Citizen Kane  [Music]  after seeing Reginald's greater plan  unfold in the season 3 finale it's no  surprise he would let out one particular  word in an almost Freudian slip  like the phrase Rosebud and Citizen Kane  the remote dropped an extreme close-up  of Reginald's lips puts tremendous  weight on the word leaving viewers  questioning its meaning comic book fans  however already know the hotel Oblivion  is an impenetrable prison built by the  monocle to hold super villains on top of  that connection the finale also revealed  to the Umbrella Academy that this  Reginald is indeed the green-blooded  cyborg alien known as the monocle  perhaps making fans even more eager for  the next volume of comics as well as  season 4 of the series based on them  eagle-eyed viewers from last season had  been anxiously awaiting the return of  young Harlan in season three after  seeing he retained Victor's immense  Powers fans speculated that this strange  old man with retro headphones a case of  cassette tapes and a suitcase full of  numbered sandwiches was indeed an older  Harlan the season 2 Cliffhanger also  teased Harlan's decimation of Sparrow's  Jamie and Alfonso as seen in season  three's third episode in his hand he's  levitating a bird which could be a  sparrow which foreshadows his explosive  Outburst that fries off the Sparrow's  faces luckily after that event viewers  received a detailed backstory depicting  the trauma Harlan endured which warped  his uncontrollable abilities it was  subsequently explained how Harlan was  able to locate the two superhuman  families his connection to these  super-powered Heroes resonated in his  mind almost like sound waves  the Umbrella Academy Season 3 brought  with it what could potentially be a  Marvel connection at least from the  standpoint of visual effects if you've  never seen the series Legion on the FX  channel it follows an extremely powerful  telepathic mutant the eponymous Legion  who struggles with mental illness as a  result of his mental state it makes it  extremely hard for him to control his  powerful abilities the Umbrella Academy  seems to be evoking the series in both  look and theme Legion shares some of the  same crew members behind the scenes such  as series composer Jeff Russo and  Director of Photography Craig robleski  this likely explains why the explosive  Outburst from Harlan at the beginning of  episode 4 is so similar to David's  kitchen utensil tornado they even look  and sound similar with cool blue tones  and chaotic whirlwinds of dangerous  objects both explosions also come from a  character's deep trauma so even if it  wasn't an intentional callback to that  other trippy superhero Tale the style  and themes definitely carry over thanks  to the talent designing and implementing  the effects  the most familiar face in the sparrow  Academy worked its way up to a brand new  ranking in season three the previous  number six in the family relentlessly  devoted himself to becoming one of the  strongest members of The Sparrows Finn's  horrific Powers allow him to unleash the  Fearsome tentacled Beast Within and it  seems his Fierce dedication has earned  him an upgrade to number two there's  already enough Bad Blood between the  Umbrella Academy and sparrows because of  the first team's arrival in the new  reality however when Ben discovers he  died in their original timeline he's far  less trustworthy of his rambunctious new  siblings after the first episode with  Marcus taken by the cougar Blitz Ben  declares himself the new number one but  in episode 3 his siblings make a passing  remark that tips off the audience that  Ben was the original number one you have  your chance once  didn't turn out too well now did it so  what did he do to get taken down a pack  was this Reginald's Twisted way of  motivating him whatever the reason his  resentment is suddenly far more  understandable  not surprisingly there are more than a  few references to the Umbrella Academy  Source material one being a new look for  fan favorite rumor after Alice and  unsuccessfully tries to rumor herself  into happiness she grabs A Shard of  broken mirror and cuts her hair short  the significance of this transformation  matches her signature style in the  comics any raver Lampman showcases a  deeply moving performance as Alison in  season three gutted to learn her  daughter Claire doesn't exist in this  timeline this sends Alison into a  downward spiral where she even rumors  Luther into wanting to stay with her  because of a desperate desire for any  sense of something familiar she also  argues with Victor about Harlan's faith  and eventually kills the old man for  what he did to The Sparrows this was  Alison's darkest season yet and it  closely resembles her comic book  counterpart  the hotel Oblivion finally makes its  frightening debut through a passageway  behind a wall-mounted Pachinko machine  located in the Buffalo Suite of the  hotel obsidian the hotel is similar to  The Overlook from The Shining albeit  bolstered with interesting additions  like a sushi Carousel murderous Samurai  Guardians and a built-in  universe-changing machine there's also  an abundance of gross cockroaches which  Lila happily squashes another comic book  reference  the biggest note of importance with the  arrival in Oblivion is the reveal of the  ambitious scheme Reginald Cooks up it  adds a necessary layer of Suspicion  which pays off when Allison kills him  the green blood and sparking metallic  skeleton is an extraordinary visual cue  one that reveals to everyone that  Reginald was not who he seemed to be it  also illustrates the Brilliance and  dedication of Reginald who purposefully  built the hotel around a portal he  discovered once the audience discovers  he is the founder of the hotel  everything begins coming together as the  maniacal Genius of the monocle is  revealed at last  potentially the deepest mystery of the  season this Easter egg is quite  intriguing unfortunately even the comics  can't help viewers much here but it does  reveal some information about The  elusive Jennifer in episode 7 after a  heated argument with Alison Victor runs  to his old room which is now bends in  the new timeline on a stable there is a  drawing of a beautiful woman with the  name Jennifer scrawled on the bottom in  the comics the Jennifer incident is a  newspaper clipping posted in space boys  base on the moon the accompanying photo  is of Luther with his hand blocking the  camera lens there are various other  clippings visible including one with the  headline the horror dead in the comics  Ben is referred to as the horror and  with this scene from the series we can  assume that the Jennifer incident and  maybe even Jennifer herself caused Ben's  death in the original timeline  the opening scene from the season 1  finale revealed Abigail Hargreaves  Reginald's love from long ago it turns  out that Luther was guarding her  cryogenically frozen corpse on the moon  though he's unaware of that fact this  adds a much deeper purpose to Luther's  time on the moon while also exposing how  selfish Reginald is to sacrifice his  son's sanity and happiness revisiting  the flashback from season one there's  another detail far more significant  after the events of the new season the  glowing orange particles that Reginald  released into the air as the Rockets  were taking off are the source of power  for all the gifted children in the  series it's also fuel for the other  worldly machine that averted the  apocalypse for the third time could  Abigail be where the particles came from  there must be another way  Abigail is Reginald's singular purpose  for every merciless action he has taken  thus far this explains his triumphant  expression in the season 3 finale when  they're finally reunited  after the kugel Blitz annihilates  everything in sight the Umbrella Academy  makes a dramatic turn and instead of the  show's usual Fade to Black in the  credits it fades to a blinding white  this stylistic Choice emphasizes the  gravity of the situation the undeniable  power of the kugelblitz and the  Beautiful sacrifice Klaus makes so he  would still be around to help his  siblings the Fade to White could also  symbolize The White Buffalo that Klaus  killed himself on the White Buffalo has  a rich and deep Native American meaning  that represents hope and abundance this  is a surprisingly comforting note to end  on after the kugelblitz devours  everything but after the Umbrella  Academy saved the world twice it's not  wise to doubt them at this point Russo's  Angelic score pauses for a brief moment  before bursting into the rousing  Umbrella Academy theme this music change  reads as a fitting call to action for  Our Heroes to save the world yet again  if there is a fourth season of The  Umbrella Academy then we'll surely play  a big part in it the cryptic after  credits scene shows Ben sitting alone on  a subway train reading while you can't  exactly make out the book he's holding  you can overhear the conductor say where  Ben is arriving Ben is writing to the  yoido train station in South Korea but  what is he doing there could this be  related to the Jennifer incident one  thing is for sure saving the world  didn't bring Ben any closer to his  siblings if he's traveling all the way  to South Korea by himself his anger is  certainly justifiable but if he stays  alone and allows it to consume him he  could suffer a fate even worse than his  original Self it's also been speculated  that this bin is in fact the  doppelganger of the sparrow version of  the character if that's the case what  does it mean about potential doubles for  the other members of the family  the plaque that commemorates the  donation of obsidian Memorial Park feels  more like a slide against the saviors of  space and time rather than a  heartwarming tribute but knowing  Reginald and after seeing his egomania  run rampant and take over the city it  probably was meant to be a middle finger  to his kids the icing on the keg of  Reginald's less than sentimental  donation is that it was donated on their  birthday right down to the year Reginald  was willing to let all seven of his  gifted children die to be reunited with  Abigail it's easy to believe he's not  above a smug gracious donation such as  this  with their powers gone and the monocle's  true nature revealed what's next for  this dysfunctional bunch of former  superheroes hopefully a fourth season  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more Looper videos about  the Umbrella Academy are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the Bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

